HST Office: narrower Home Paragraph (Writer, Slides) and Font (Slides), so Paragraph stays at 1485 px.

Paragraph's toolboxes are already icon-only, so its only smaller ladder state was its button: at 1485 px
Slides showed Paragraph as a button. Its width came from the indent column, which also held Find & Replace
and Select All. Both move to the first row of the last column, whose second row is already as wide
(Writer: beside the hidden text direction buttons, above shading, borders, sort and formatting marks;
Slides: beside text direction, above the vertical text alignment), about 50 px narrower. In Slides, Change
Case moves from the font name row to the end of the second row, under the size box, about 30 px narrower.
No command is removed; ids are unchanged.

